{
 "deltas": [
  {
   "id": "W0",
   "name": "widget fetch time",
   "text": "the fixtures carry no response time a widget would have seen, so every scenario states a plausible last widget refresh 2 to 3 minutes before its clock (Last updated HH:MM). The times, platforms and lines are the fixture’s."
  },
  {
   "id": "W1",
   "name": "late lead",
   "text": "the home exemplar’s own `tight` state: the 09:24 leaves 5 min late (09:29) and reaches Town Hall at 09:56, 2 min before the unchanged 09:58 T4, so the trip still arrives 10:08."
  },
  {
   "id": "W2",
   "name": "cancelled lead",
   "text": "the 09:24 is cancelled (home delta D8); the widget answers with the 09:39, the next real service in the same fixture."
  },
  {
   "id": "W3",
   "name": "offline retained",
   "text": "the widget’s refresh at 09:20 failed; it shows the app’s last board for the pair, saved 09:02, whose times are the fixture’s."
  },
  {
   "id": "W4",
   "name": "pinned",
   "text": "the rider pinned the 09:39 at 09:15 (pinned before departure), and pinned the 09:24 for the under-way frame, shown at 09:33 on the first leg."
  },
  {
   "id": "W5",
   "name": "evening way home",
   "text": "home deltas D1-D3: the repo has no Bondi Junction -> Rhodes fixture, so the real outbound shape runs in reverse +9 h at 18:12, with no invented headsign or change platforms."
  },
  {
   "id": "W6",
   "name": "no services",
   "text": "at 01:10 the API is taken to have answered with no journeys for the pair, which is when the product prints `No services in the next few hours`."
  },
  {
   "id": "W7",
   "name": "longest names",
   "text": "a MEASUREMENT, not a journey: the two widest names in the 423-station index (web/stations.json) replace Rhodes and Bondi Junction on the real 09:24."
  },
  {
   "id": "W8",
   "name": "widest values",
   "text": "a MEASUREMENT, not a journey: the widest legal value of every track at once — 99 min, 12 MIN LATE, Platform 12, the longest real headsign (Mount Victoria via Parramatta) — on the Central -> Parramatta pair."
  },
  {
   "id": "W9",
   "name": "scheduled-only tail",
   "text": "at 10:18 the fixture holds only two later services (both without realtime); a missing third row is the fixture ending, not the end of service."
  }
